      "problem": "Find the inverse of the function $f(x) = bx-5,$ where $b$ is a constant.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the inverse of a function, we follow the four steps below.\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y.$\n\n$$\ny = bx- 5\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y.$\n\n$$\nx = by- 5\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =by-5 \\\\ x+5 & =by \\\\ \\frac{x+5}{b} & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with $f^{-1}(x).$\n\n$$\nf^{-1}(x) = \\dfrac{x + 5}{b}\n$$",
